  "status": "completed",
  "output": "The edit introduced a real problem: a literal newline was inserted instead of the two characters `\\` and `n`. As a result, the file is now malformed and fails with `unexpected EOF while looking for matching '`.\n\nTo restore the file to exactly the requested content, I'll rewrite it with just that one line changed:Line 3 is now exactly `IFS=$'\\n'` (verified with `od -c`: `I F S = $ ' \\ n '`), and the file passes `bash -n`.\n\nOne caveat about the intent, since only that line was allowed to change:\n\n- `read -r -a parts <<< \"$1\"` **stops at the first newline** in `$1`, so with newline-splitting the array will only ever contain the first line. Testing with `$'a\\nb\\nc'` prints `[a]` only.\n- If you actually want one entry per line, the `read` line would need to change too, e.g. `mapfile -t parts <<< \"$1\"` (note `mapfile` keeps the trailing comma-separated fields intact but drops the final empty line).\n\nLet me know if you want that follow-up change; otherwise the file is exactly as specified.",
